    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1150,
        20
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        720
      ],
      "order": 28,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Anima Two-Character Regional Hires-Fix + Turbo\n\nThis graph generates both characters in the same diffusion trajectory. Anima Turbo v0.2 is loaded globally once and feeds both passes. Each character receives its own complete prompt and model-only character LoRA through a freely positioned soft regional mask. These masks are influence maps inside one latent, not separately rendered images. Any area outside both masks uses the unhooked shared-scene default conditioning.\n\n## Use\n1. Describe the complete shared scene and interaction in the green node.\n2. Select Character A and B. Their manifest triggers are injected automatically. Add visible hair, eyes, clothes, expression, and body direction in each details field.\n3. Move each live A/B center and adjust its width and height. Keep a feathered overlap where hands or bodies interact.\n4. Keep the global Turbo loader enabled, then queue. The same Turbo model and regional conditioning are used in both passes.\n\n## Quality defaults\n- Turbo LoRA: strength 1.00. Reduce toward 0.70 if the result is too rigid or stylized.\n- Both passes: 12 steps, CFG 1, Euler/simple. CFG 1 ignores the negative prompt; try CFG 1.5-2.0 when negatives are important.\n- Regional mode: `default` gives each character full-image context, then blends only its masked prediction.\n- Character LoRA: start at 0.80; tune roughly 0.65-0.95.\n- Feather: 4-10 percent. Increase for soft interaction; reduce if identities mix.\n- Hires-fix: AnimeSharp 4x, Lanczos to effective 1.5x, then denoise 0.38. Tune 0.32-0.42.\n\n## Requirements\n- Current ComfyUI core with CreateHookLoraModelOnly and ConditioningSetProperties.\n- WAI-ANIMA or Anima Base, qwen_3_06b_base, qwen_image_vae.\n- anima-turbo-lora-v0.2.safetensors under models/loras.\n- 4x-AnimeSharp.pth or another anime ESRGAN model.\n- Two installed character LoRAs listed in config/anima-loras.json.\n\nTurbo is the only global LoRA. Do not place both character LoRAs in a global loader; that defeats regional identity separation."
      ],
      "title": "Read first",
      "flags": {},
      "mode": 0
    }
